# VeritasAI Phase 5 — Security & Deployment Walkthrough

## Changes Made

### Server Hardening ([server/index.js](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/server/index.js))
- **3 separate rate limiters**: Global (200/15min), Analyze (15/hr, skipped for auth users), Auth (10/15min)
- **2MB body limit** (down from 50MB — files go through multer, not JSON body)
- **`/api/health`** endpoint returning status, timestamp, version
- **Cleanup job** runs every 30 min + at startup (deletes uploads older than 1 hour)
- **JWT_SECRET warning** at boot if missing or < 32 chars

### New File: [cleanup.js](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/server/lib/cleanup.js)
Deletes stale uploaded files older than 1 hour, skips dotfiles.

### SSRF & Input Sanitization ([analyze.js](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/server/routes/analyze.js))
- Blocks bare private IPs (10.x, 127.x, 192.168.x, 169.254.x, 172.16-31.x)
- Blocks `file://`, `ftp://`, `javascript://` protocols
- Rejects hostnames < 4 chars
- URL trimmed, max 2000 chars
- tempFileId validated: only `[a-zA-Z0-9_\-.]` allowed (prevents path traversal)

### File Upload Security ([upload.js](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/server/routes/upload.js))
- Filename sanitization (blocks `..`, `/`, `\`)
- Explicit `LIMIT_FILE_SIZE` error message
- Enhanced file-type rejection message

### Auth Timing Attack Fix ([auth.js](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/server/routes/auth.js))
- `bcrypt.compare` always runs against a dummy hash when user not found

### Security Meta Tags (all 5 HTML files)
- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
- `referrer: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`

### Deployment Files & Git Config
- [Procfile](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/Procfile), [.env.example](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/.env.example), [README.md](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/README.md)
- [uploads/.gitkeep](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/uploads/.gitkeep), [db/.gitkeep](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/db/.gitkeep) and corresponding [.gitignore](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/.gitignore) files to keep the app stateless while tracking structure
- Root [.gitignore](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/.gitignore) correctly ignores [.env](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/.env) and `node_modules`
- [frameExtract.js](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/Vertias/server/lib/frameExtract.js) supports dynamic `FFMPEG_PATH` for hosting platforms like Railway.

